Subject: [PATCH] arc: 0007-real-token-truncation (count tool-output budgets with
 the served model's tokenizer)

`tool_output_tokenizer = "/path/tokenizer.json"` makes every token budget of
`codex-utils-output-truncation` real tokens of that HF tokenizer instead of
`bytes / 4`. An unknown model slug falls back to a byte policy, so
`tool_output_token_limit = 2500` used to mean 10,000 bytes, about 10k tokens of
grid hex. With the key set the limit is a token policy, over-budget output keeps
the first half and the last half of the budget (cut on char boundaries, both
sides re-counted) and the marker reports the real number of tokens removed.

- Covered: `truncate_text`, `formatted_truncate_text`, content items, function
  output payloads (exec, shell, MCP, code mode, history recording), unified exec
  `Original token count` and its response-size loop.
- Fail fast: an unreadable/invalid file or a missing `tool_output_token_limit`
  fails config loading. Loaded once per process; a second, different path errors.
- Unset: no code path changes.
---

